@startuml review_03_stratified_multivar
' Review unit 03 of 15 -- see docs/review_diagrams.md for the series.
' State AFTER commits 08e0cfa, 4aac88d, c0393ef (src +564/-127, tests +87/-32).
' Every number below is from a run of the two cases at commit c0393ef.
' Render: plantuml docs/review_03_stratified_multivar.puml

title Unit 03 -- per-stratum placement for every variable (08e0cfa..c0393ef)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FCFCFC
  BorderColor #777777
  DiamondBackgroundColor #F2F2F2
  DiamondBorderColor #777777
}
skinparam partition {
  BorderColor #8899AA
  FontColor #33495E
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDF0
  BorderColor #C8C08A
}

start

partition "the call -- unchanged parameters, two cases" {
  :GenerateData(
     num_obs=100, num_dims=3, ratio_dims=[1, 2, 2],
     density=[0.4, 0.1], seed=77,
     num_vars=2, var_dims=[3, 2],
     overlap=0.5, fixed_overlap=False,
     <b>case A</b>: max_obs=None      <b>case B</b>: max_obs=40)
  .generate(netcdf_filepath, parquet_filepath, parquet_tmp);
}

partition "validators/ and config/" {
  :shape [4, 8, 8], 256 sites, density_zero 0.0625, num_obs 102
  var_num_obs 102 and 26, var_dims_indices [ [0,1,2], [0,2] ] as before
  var1 constant on x1, pinned at index 2, overlap_target 0.5;
  #C8E6C9:<b>_choose_split_dim</b> replaces plain argmax
  shared = the dimensions EVERY variable varies along: 0 and 2
  largest of those -> <b>dim_split = 2</b>  (was 1)
  prints: "Stratifying along dimension 2 (size 8) rather than the
  largest dimension 1 (size 8), which is not shared by every variable";
  note right #C8E6C9
    Overlap is measured on the dimensions two variables
    share. If a variable were constant along the split
    axis its projection would collapse across strata,
    and a per-stratum target could not add up to the
    requested global one. Excluding such an axis can
    mean splitting a shorter one, which lowers the
    maximum number of chunks.
  end note
  :case A: NTASKS 1. case B: NTASKS 3 along x2,
  section_sizes 3, 3, 2 and div_points 0, 3, 6, 8;
}

partition "coordinates (both cases)" {
  :one RNG per axis, x0 4 values, x1 8 values, x2 8 values, sorted;
}

partition "placement -- MultiVarRecordGenerator.generate_multivar_stratified" {
  #FFCDD2:generate_with_overlap: one global choice for var0, then
  round(target * var_i's own count) cells taken from the reference and
  the remainder taken from anywhere, so accidental coincidences
  landed on top of the target;
  #C8E6C9:<b>var0 first, by the unit-02 routine</b>
  generate_stratified_indices(global_shape, num_obs=102,
     seed, split_dim=2, strata)
  LHS stage now takes <b>n_s = max(shape) = 8</b>, not min(shape) = 4;
  note right #C8E6C9
    generate_lhs_indices raises if n_s < max(shape):
    each point uses one coordinate per axis, so fewer
    than max(shape) points must leave some coordinate
    of the longest axis unused -- a grid line carrying
    no data, which the definition of the grid excludes.
    Measured: var0's per-stratum counts go from
    12, 11, 14, 15, 8, 10, 17, 15 to
    <b>12, 12, 13, 13, 13, 13, 13, 13</b>
  end note
  #C8E6C9:<b>per-variable geometry, computed once</b>
  for var1: dims it shares with the strata = [0] (x2 is the split axis)
  plane = 4 cells per stratum
  var1 varies along x2, so it lives in EVERY stratum
  counts = apportion(26, weights=plane per stratum)
  -> <b>3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 4, 4</b>;
  note right #C8E6C9
    If a variable is CONSTANT on the split axis it lives
    in exactly one stratum: weights are zero everywhere
    except its home stratum, so every other chunk places
    nothing for it. That is why _select_constant_coords
    is now given the GLOBAL shape -- handed a chunk's
    task shape it drew the coordinate from [0, task_size)
    and each chunk pinned the variable somewhere else.
  end note
  #C8E6C9:<b>per stratum j, per variable i</b>
  proj = var0's cells in stratum j, seen through var_i's dims
  free_cells = plane - |proj|
  lo = max(0, n_here - free_cells)     forced: nowhere else to go
  hi = min(n_here, |proj|)             cannot exceed either set
  n_overlap = clip(round(t_i * |proj|), lo, hi)
  fixed_overlap False -> draw from proj with default_rng([seed, VAR=10, i, j])
  fixed_overlap True  -> draw from one shared permutation,
     default_rng([seed, SHARED_OVERLAP=11, j])
  remainder drawn from cells held by NEITHER variable, via _ranks_to_local
  values from the same VAR stream, after the sites;
  note right #C8E6C9
    The target is now a share of the REFERENCE footprint
    (F1), evaluated inside the stratum, so no worker needs
    the global denominator. A clipped stratum is reported:
    "WARNING var1: overlap target not reachable in N of 8
    strata ... Density takes precedence."
    _ranks_to_local is also vectorised in this unit:
    searchsorted-style shifting instead of a Python loop
    over the excluded sites.
  end note
}

if (NTASKS) then (== 1  -- CASE A, serial)
  #FFF9C4:measured at this commit
  var0 102 sites, per-stratum on x2: 12, 12, 13, 13, 13, 13, 13, 13
  var1  26 sites, per-stratum on x2:  3,  3,  3,  3,  3,  3,  4,  4
  in every stratum |proj(var0)| = 4 and var1 takes 3 or 4 of them
  shared dims (x0, x2): |proj0| = 32, |proj1| = 26, intersection 26
  reported overlap (still the pooled full-space number) <b>0.3846</b>
  the same data read as F1 is 26/32 = 0.8125
  parquet grows to <b>118 rows</b> (was 114), ds.nc 12589 B;
else (== 3  -- CASE B, parallel)
  #C8E6C9:workers are now handed the GLOBAL var_num_obs
  and derive their own per-stratum counts, instead of
  being handed a pre-split per-chunk count;
  #FFF9C4:chunk files split along x2:
  ds_0.nc 12290 B (x0 4, x1 8, x2 3) var0 37, var1 9
  ds_1.nc 12290 B (x0 4, x1 8, x2 3) var0 39, var1 9
  ds_2.nc 12290 B (x0 4, x1 8, x2 2) var0 26, var1 8
  totals 102 and 26, matching serial;
endif

partition "the single-variable flow (num_vars=1, density=0.4)" {
  #FFE0B2:touched: the LHS stage now takes max(shape) = 8 points
  instead of 4, so the placement changes again
  serial per-stratum counts 12, 12, 13, 13, 13, 13, 13, 13
  parallel chunk counts 37, 39, 26 (were 38, 38, 26)
  num_obs < max(shape) is now an error rather than a silent
  grid with unused coordinates;
}

stop

legend right
  |<#C8E6C9> green |= added or changed by THIS unit |
  |<#FFCDD2> red |= removed by THIS unit |
  |<#FFE0B2> orange |= single-variable flow touched by THIS unit |
  |<#FFF9C4> yellow |= generated data or file that changed as a result |
  | plain | unchanged since unit 02 |

  <b>What to review in unit 03</b>
  * _choose_split_dim and the empty-intersection error
  * generate_multivar_stratified: the lo/hi clipping, the
    "neither variable" remainder, and the per-stratum rounding
    drift (order sqrt(num_strata)/2 on the global numerator)
  * n_s = max(shape) and the new ValueError paths
  * _select_constant_coords on the GLOBAL shape
  * _ranks_to_local vectorisation -- same results as the loop?
  <b>Verified</b>: both variables now spread across every stratum;
  serial and parallel totals agree (102 and 26).
end legend

@enduml
